{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 16 (stretch 3, hard pass; S4 pacing): a crown of stones. Seven capturable stones (two ley, three ward, two seer) sit on a rotationally symmetric continent, and two wolf packs den by the north seer and the southwestern ward. Staged prayer chain: take the western ley, clear both packs (which wakes the dormant crown ward), take the crown (which wakes the north seer, already held by the sneaky rival), pray the seer away, keep six of the seven stones at once for two minutes while the rival prays them back and raids, then raze the eastern Hearth (a destroy, not eliminateAll). The rival is hard but capped at 14 troops; its village is a fort (four watchtowers, twelve posted wardens), three more posted wardens arrive every 100 s from minute 4 until the north seer falls (until 3, so a slow player faces a bigger fort but the spawn is bounded; unbounded it stalemated bot offset 12 in the hold), and fourteen more dig in around the Hearth when the hold is done. Bot (offset 1) wins about 20500; offsets 0, 3, 7, 12 win by 36000 of the 54000 limit.",
